{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788029801347522291,"compiled_state":{"alias":"luminous-stenchful-cottontail","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"46847e34ada74d513c87f47cd2b9669e16e4d080a37e0e380ed18189f455bf22","event_uuid":"85ec436e-a1b6-457e-bf11-094ebd7c582a","position":{"commit_sha":"7a76f368dd398430d4b069c6c863895073ef85cc","position":"1788026457668319415-85ec436e-a1b6-457e-bf11-094ebd7c582a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"4c0a59f7d3e19b895a570fa383d96135c9130580a5a47848032f55c8eaadd40a","event_uuid":"3657b3e2-c118-44de-8257-6b86d40305dc","position":{"commit_sha":"b77c35a05b1c052bf8a4352a557c828c5b894b48","position":"1788026506200068825-3657b3e2-c118-44de-8257-6b86d40305dc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"6bdd5df38c540c1e6ce97e62df97cddd96ddfcaa8b324c42fc64e99544565750","event_uuid":"2ea01154-4571-4342-9779-4f641e632689","position":{"commit_sha":"85e1070372e5a9ac2edda4ed8b41a0fb898fcb9a","position":"1788026607461994107-2ea01154-4571-4342-9779-4f641e632689"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7fa768e5f03453309e3021cf3d34da784c2d77aa57e4f12d5123d77576be0fd3","event_uuid":"67dfc94a-4f48-4b04-b183-8b48db6df3e8","position":{"commit_sha":"cd365109597a88532432e94723acc86dafd47582","position":"1788026790317907233-67dfc94a-4f48-4b04-b183-8b48db6df3e8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788026457668319415,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3657b3e2-c118-44de-8257-6b86d40305dc","relation":"blocks","target_id":"ec44-b572-1067-4c52"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nADR 0098 defines one immutable non-secret `OperationSnapshot` per operation. Today CLI and shared command-write entry points still call `emit_shadow_snapshot()`, while store/config helpers can resolve ambient state independently. The reconciler runtime already demonstrates snapshot-derived bindings; reuse that pattern.\n\nThis story cuts ordinary CLI, MCP/Python command, and store-opening operations over. LLM-specific resolution is the dependent follow-up.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Census the command/store consumers and identify the public composition boundaries for CLI, MCP, and Python.\n- Compose exactly once after input parsing and before lock/network/write, then pass focused immutable projections/context through shared command/store seams.\n- Preserve explicit-input > environment > project > user > schema precedence and independent repository-root selection from ADR 0098.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic and effect-spy tests.\n- Remove migrated shadow calls and ambient reloads; extend the existing ownership checker with red-proven detections rather than a second registry.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` and `src/rebar/config.py` — existing composer/projections and approved compatibility boundary.\n- `src/rebar/_cli/`, `src/rebar/_commands/`, `src/rebar/_store/`, and MCP command entry modules — compose once and thread focused context.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/` and focused config/store/CLI/MCP tests.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and its exact exception registry.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: equivalent CLI, MCP, and Python operations resolve one identical snapshot and produce existing effects. Metamorphic edge: mutate environment, selected files, and CWD after capture; the active operation remains unchanged and the next operation changes. Failure edge: malformed selected configuration causes zero lock, subprocess, network, or store effects.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Representative CLI, MCP, and Python ticket/store reads and writes each compose one snapshot/context, proven by call-count tests through production entry points.\n- [ ] Given environment/config/CWD mutation after composition, the active operation's selected tracker directory, branch, remote, push mode, and observable effects remain unchanged; a new operation observes the change.\n- [ ] Explicit operation input remains authoritative and malformed selected config fails before lock, subprocess, network, or store write.\n- [ ] Store helpers receive focused projections/context and do not call `load_config`, environment, or CWD beneath the approved boundary.\n- [ ] Migrated `emit_shadow_snapshot` calls and compatibility resolution branches are deleted, with no stored ticket/event/bridge format change.\n- [ ] The structural ownership checker catches a synthetic below-boundary ambient read and has zero new legacy exceptions.\n- [ ] Existing config, tracker layout, concurrency, CLI/MCP/library parity, lint, typecheck, and default suites pass.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_operation_config.py","reason":"Behavior-bearing snapshot/context composition."},{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Central config projection and approved boundary compatibility."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/","reason":"Compose once per CLI invocation."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/","reason":"Thread command/store projections."},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/","reason":"Consume store configuration without ambient reload."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp","reason":"Compose once per MCP operation."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/","reason":"Consumer-level cross-surface metamorphic tests."},{"path":"scripts/check_config_ownership.py","reason":"Structural prevention of below-boundary reads."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","ec44-b572-1067-4c52"],["parent","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["configuration","store","migration"],"ticket_id":"3a08-4016-0a3a-4be0","ticket_type":"story","title":"Make OperationSnapshot authoritative for CLI, command, and store operations","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["85ec436e-a1b6-457e-bf11-094ebd7c582a","3657b3e2-c118-44de-8257-6b86d40305dc","2ea01154-4571-4342-9779-4f641e632689","67dfc94a-4f48-4b04-b183-8b48db6df3e8"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788029801347522291,"uuid":"e7910f00-f48d-49c6-821d-bc3d34b9acdf"}